      "writtenOn": "2023-10-08T12:01:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done, but I don\u0027t think the comment in the build file is useful.\n\nThe fundamental problem here is that\n- It\u0027s expensive to even figure out what rule is trying to build this, not to mention why it\u0027s built or what its dependencies are\n- The dependencies are completely splintered and it\u0027s impossible to deduce from their name what they contain, or from the path of a file in what target(s) it\u0027s contained and under what form (full/stub)\n- It\u0027s nearly impossible to understand what the difference between `X-pre-jarjar` and `X.impl`\n- Any change in the build file mean a multiple-minute wait at next build\n\nMy complaint is about how expensive it is to figure out. I know and understand the unzip way. I\u0027m trying to avoid people having to do this ; I spent 4 hours of work on this and timed out before I resorted to that. If you\u0027re so deep in this that you\u0027re looking inside the jars, you have figured out all the dependency graph already and have an understanding of what *should* be where. It takes hours just to get there. I want to find ways to stop wasting developers\u0027 time this way.\n\nNote that no – someone who doesn\u0027t understand why a solution works is in no place to help write what kind of info would have helped. I wrote a comment, you gave me an idea in response, I tried it, it worked, I didn\u0027t know why. This gives me a fish ; I don\u0027t want to learn to fish, I want to post dead simple instructions next to the fishing spot so other people don\u0027t have to come to you to learn how to fish. I am no closer to know how to do that.",
      "parentUuid": "f2f95f07_413c7a9f",
